WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.391
One sign-in, three roles. Customers register, verify email, or reset a forgotten password. This tour uses synthetic accounts, with all
credentials hidden.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:22.175
Customer sign-in opens only their own orders. My orders separates active, completed, and action-needed requests, with status and next
steps.

3
00:00:22.792 --> 00:00:31.862
New order selects Internet, SD-WAN, or Cloud Connect, city, address, contact, language, notification channel, and frequency.

4
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:40.765
Open an order for the five-step tracker, installation details, and update history. Progress appears automatically.

5
00:00:41.375 --> 00:00:49.225
When information is missing, confirm or correct the installation site and contact preferences to release the hold.

6
00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:57.658
Profile updates name, company, mobile, language, and password. Changing a password revokes earlier sessions.

7
00:00:58.292 --> 00:01:06.238
Guests can place orders and track with a private code. Customers can link an existing order using its tracking proof.

8
00:01:06.875 --> 00:01:14.394
Partners first accept a staff invitation and choose a password, then use the same email-and-password sign-in.

9
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:24.043
Deliveries shows only their organisation's orders, expected dates, on-track or delayed status, progress, and actions needed.

10
00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:32.858
Update the address, preferred date, access notes, and purchase-order reference. Confirming the site can restart a held order.

11
00:01:33.458 --> 00:01:43.018
Payments tracks outstanding, overdue, and paid balances, invoice amounts, VAT, terms, due dates, and payment references. No money
moves.

12
00:01:43.625 --> 00:01:51.056
Raise delivery, billing, technical, or other concerns, link an order, and follow replies until resolved.

13
00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:57.884
Account changes name, mobile, language, and password; billing terms remain read-only.

14
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:08.206
Service staff use the access-token form here. Separate single-sign-on deployments use Microsoft work accounts and role-based
permissions.

15
00:02:08.833 --> 00:02:17.469
The control tower summarises orders, activations, exceptions, and recoveries across Istanbul, Ankara, and Izmir.

16
00:02:18.083 --> 00:02:25.453
Order workspace brings every enterprise journey together. Select an order to inspect its full execution.

17
00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:37.037
Detail links events, tool calls, service and resource orders, capacity reservations, and customer updates. Advisory AI never executes
changes.

18
00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:46.487
Exception desk holds route conflicts and closed change windows for human approval or rejection. Staff can also correct sites.

19
00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:55.870
Create operator or partner orders, select scenarios, and check simulated capacity through authenticated MCP.

20
00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:06.525
Add partners and invite people; manage terms, billing, API-channel mapping, invitations, suspension, and recorded or reversed payments.

21
00:03:07.125 --> 00:03:13.247
The concerns inbox lets staff reply, change status, and resolve partner questions.

22
00:03:13.875 --> 00:03:19.044
Validate checks address, feasibility, and inventory before work starts.

23
00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:24.957
Decompose turns the product request into linked service and resource work.

24
00:03:25.583 --> 00:03:32.579
Provision reserves capacity once and orchestrates simulated network, cloud, and wholesale tasks.

25
00:03:33.208 --> 00:03:42.370
Recover diagnoses allowlisted faults and retries once; unknown faults or policy conflicts remain under human control.

26
00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:51.575
Communicate sends English or Turkish updates, respects notification preferences, and handles reminders and escalation.

27
00:03:52.208 --> 00:04:03.344
Each agent tab shows queued orders, action counts, holds, latest tools, and activity outcomes. The supervisor coordinates durable,
event-driven handoffs.

28
00:04:03.958 --> 00:04:12.726
Analytics compares average, median, slowest-ten-percent delivery time, and fallout against seven-day and eight-percent targets.

29
00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:24.106
Agent timing separates queue wait from processing, excluding human waits. Outcome and scenario charts expose bottlenecks and
automatic recoveries.

30
00:04:24.708 --> 00:04:35.430
Choose live orders, benchmarks, or both. Run fifty or one hundred isolated synthetic orders; fewer than thirty decided orders remain
indicative.

31
00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:46.280
Data source shows storage and reporting synchronisation. Simulator timings and benchmark assumptions are not proof of real carrier
performance.

32
00:04:46.917 --> 00:05:02.882
Trust and governance explains safety boundaries and provenance. Filter and export the audit. Authenticated APIs expose TM
Forum-inspired interfaces; walkthrough links explain architecture. Sessions stay separate per tab.

33
00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:12.034
Three tailored experiences, one traceable workflow. All service provisioning and invoice payments shown here are simulated.
